  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant will support the Zamara Foundation, a Kenyan feminist organization advancing the sexual and reproductive health, rights, and justice (SRHRJ) of adolescent girls and young women in all their diversities throughout East Africa. The Zamara Foundation employs a multipronged strategy that includes intersectional feminist leadership training and consciousness-raising, creating safe and brave spaces for coalition building, using digital and print media to advance SRHRJ, and influencing policy change and reform through advocacy and community dialogue forums. (Strategy: Global Reproductive Equity)</narrative>
  </description>
